#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:5 347ddbc37e0847889df3ac88e1562fd2
msgid "交互式作业提交srun"
msgstr "Interactive Job Submission with srun"

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:7 8f920dee91b14d4c9f65dae0e7a9d92d
msgid ""
"Slurm作业通常分为交互式和批量式两种。 交互式作业通常用于代码编译、脚本调试、交互式计算等工作。 长期后台计算的任务通常以作业脚本的方式进行批量提交"
" :ref:`sbatch` 。"
msgstr ""
"Slurm jobs are usually divided into interactive and batch. Interactive jobs "
"are usually used for code compilation, script debugging, interactive "
"computing, etc. Long-term background computing tasks are usually submitted "
"in batch by job scripts."

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:12 100e0d44462b4d3d89cac33e059e16ce
msgid "简介"
msgstr "Introduction"

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:14 86060224213b4a2fb5865dadf01673e7
msgid "交互式提交作业：在shell窗口中执行 ``srun`` 命令，主要命令格式如下："
msgstr ""
"Interactive Job Submission: Execute the srun command in a shell window. The "
"main command format is as follows:"

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:22 a410ce2d4b894a47a83e73ba092e5960
msgid "srun常用选项"
msgstr "Common srun Options"

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:24 d05817583f5347338a8344d89b344191
msgid "srun包括多个选项，其中最常用的选项主要有以下几个："
msgstr ""
"srun has several options, with the most commonly used options including the "
"following:"

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:26 de10bb17ec8c47ac81e72e0fde8c8b4f
msgid "-n, --ntasks=number 指定要运行的任务数。请求为number 个任务分配资源，默认为每个任务一个处理器核"
msgstr ""
"-n, --ntasks=number Specifies the number of tasks to run. Requests "
"allocation of resources for 'number' tasks, with the default being one "
"processor core per task"

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:27 ff8e18f24ddc472ea9d1e68feb1fc774
msgid ""
"-c, --cpus-per-task=ncpus 告知资源管理系统控制进程，作业步的每个任务需要ncpus "
"个处理器核。若未指定此选项，则控制进程默认为每个任务分配一个处理器核。"
msgstr ""
"-c, --cpus-per-task=ncpus Informs the resource management system that each "
"task in the job step requires 'ncpus' processor cores.If this option is not "
"specified, the control process defaults to allocating one processor core per"
" task."

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:28 31eec3cadf704483a1f37141d3bcbbdd
msgid "-N, --nodes=minnodes[-maxnodes]"
msgstr "-N, --nodes=minnodes[-maxnodes]"

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:29 9a7aa6dc2ed5464fb74f2f353c442f1b
msgid ""
"请求为作业至少分配minnodes个节点。调度器可能觉得在多于 "
"minnodes个节点上运行作业。可以通过maxnodes限制最多分配的节点数目（例如“-N 2-4”或“--nodes=2-4”）。最少和最多节点数目"
" 可以相同以指定特定的节点数目（例如，“-N 2”或“--nodes=2-2” 将请求两个且仅两个节点）。分区的节点数目限制将覆盖作业的请求。 "
"如果作业的节点限制超出了分区中配置的节点数目，作业将被拒绝。 如果没有指定-N，缺省行为是分配足够多的节点以满足-n和-c参数的 "
"需求。在允许的限制范围内以及不延迟作业开始运行的前提下，作业将被分配尽可能多的节点。"
msgstr ""
"Requests at least 'minnodes' nodes for the job. The scheduler may choose to "
"run the job on more than 'minnodes' nodes. The maximum number of nodes "
"allocated can be limited by using 'maxnodes' (e.g., '-N 2-4' or '--"
"nodes=2-4'). The minimum and maximum node counts can be the same to specify "
"a specific number of nodes (e.g., '-N 2' or '--nodes=2-2' requests exactly "
"two nodes). Node count constraints for partitions override job requests. If "
"the job's node request exceeds the number of nodes configured in the "
"partition, the job will be denied. If '-N' is not specified, the default "
"behavior is to allocate enough nodes to satisfy the requirements of '-n' and"
" '-c' parameterswithin the allowed constraints and without delaying the "
"start of the job, maximizing the number of nodes allocated as much as "
"possible."

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:30 4ac98c37717643ae81c7cc96ade434cc
msgid "-p, --partition=partition name 在指定分区中分配资源。如未指定，则由控制进程在系统默认分区中分配资源。"
msgstr ""
"-p, --partition=partition name Allocates resources within the specified "
"partition. If not specified, the control process allocates resources in the "
"system's default partition."

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:31 077cc5c0ec334a0eb5af416d5d99d180
msgid ""
"-w, --nodelist=node name list "
"请求指定的节点名字列表。作业分配资源中将至少包含这些节点。列表可以用逗号分隔的节点名或节点范围（如cpu[01-05,07,...]，其中cpu为节点名称）指定，或者用"
" 文件名指定。如果参数中包含“/”字符，则会被当作文件名。如果指定了最大节点数如-N 1-2，但是文件中有多余2个节点，则请求列 表中只使用前2个节点。"
msgstr ""
"-w, --nodelist=node name list Requests a specific list of node names. The "
"job allocation will include at least these nodes. The list may be comma-"
"separated node names or node ranges (e.g., cpu[01-05,07,...], where cpu is "
"the node name prefix), or a file name. If the argument contains a ``/`` "
"character, it is treated as a file name. If a maximum node count is "
"specified (e.g., ``-N 1-2``) but the file lists more than two nodes, only "
"the first two nodes in the request list are used."

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:32 16e63b18655d4cb891071490efa631c1
msgid "-x, --exclude=node name list"
msgstr "-x, --exclude=node name list"

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:33 3259a3db701a430ea93c06f2aa16ee21
msgid ""
"不要将指定的节点分配给作业。如果包含“/”字符，参数将被当作 文件名。srun将把作业请求提交到控制进程，然后在远程节点上启动 "
"所有进程。如果资源请求不能立即被满足，srun将阻塞等待，直到资源可用以运行作业。如果指定了--immediate选项，则srun将在资源 "
"不是立即可用时终止。"
msgstr ""
"Do not assign specific nodes to the job. If the parameter contains '/' "
"character, it will be treated as a filename. srun will submit the job "
"request to the control process and then initiate all processes on remote "
"nodes.If the resource request cannot be immediately satisfied, srun will "
"block and wait until resources become available to run the job. If the "
"--immediate option is specified,srun will terminate when resources are not "
"immediately available."

#: ../../docs/jobs/slurm-srun.rst:34 39b3829ee42f44289933cc3561372b00
msgid "-h, --help 若需使用srun更多选项，可通过“srun –h”或“srun --help”查看."
msgstr ""
"-h, --help For more srun options, you can view them by running 'srun -h' or "
"'srun --help' "

